      "writtenOn": "2026-07-31T08:08:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is the rd_lock meant to be keeping out here? Its only three users in the tree are __direct_lpi_inv, its_vpe_4_1_invall_locked and its_vpe_get_vsgi_state, none of which touch GICR_CTLR, GICR_PROPBASER or GICR_PENDBASER, and all three are already unreachable under pKVM because the GICv4 patch clears has_direct_lpi, has_vlpis and has_rvpeid.\n\nSo as far as I can tell we hold IRQs off across the whole deprivilege loop and get nothing back. Worth settling, because if the driver\u0027s own locks are not what closes the pre-init window then the pre-init handler table is carrying it alone.",
      "revId": "c9223f9535911a698deadec41f3d8d022c9f5d20",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
